.TH CHTTPCLIENT_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_destroy \- destroy an HTTP client and NULL the handle
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

chttpclient_destroy(cli)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Macro wrapper around __chttpclient_destroy.  Waits for all in-flight
requests to complete, frees all resources, then sets cli to NULL.

"All in-flight requests" spans every tier: a synchronous
chttpclient_do/_streaming call still executing on another thread, and
any chttpclient_do_async/_streaming or chttpclient_do_pooled/
_streaming request submitted to the shared reactor engine that has
not yet completed and is not merely sitting idle-pooled.  It is safe
to call this even if a ctpool_future returned by chttpclient_do_async/
_streaming has not been waited on yet.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli   An lvalue of type chttpcli.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR __chttpclient_destroy (3),
.BR ___chttpclient_destroy (3),
.BR create_chttpclient (3),
.BR chttp_default_client (3)
